summary: 'Crossed from discussion into architecture for the Classroom agent-learning model (decision TD-2026-06-19-007). Loid designed the learning-loop core (failure→reinforcement flow) and Cid designed the artifacts/skill surface; combined into docs/specs/classroom.md. KEYSTONE DE-RISK: attribution is HALF-BUILT — the apply-side already exists (notebook-refs.jsonl records injected entries; incrementApplied bumps appliedCount, orchestration.ts:1284-1298); the only gap is the fail-side reducer + making orchestrationId the required join key (application-receipt ↔ break ↔ outcome). Down-revision solved via the existing latest-wins/no-ratchet path + an anti-gaming guard (can''t attribute a break to an entry never loaded). Mostly REUSE: protocol machinery backs .syllabus; the jsonl-instrument shape backs classroom-certifications.jsonl + field-failures.jsonl; one additive provenance change (''external''). MVP turns the full loop once on the cheapest signal (reviewer/human verdicts). University + nevr.land updates sequenced after the MVP proves the model. 8 open questions captured in the spec (orchestrationId provenance + peer-assessor selection are load-bearing).'
